WEBVTT

00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:00.120
Ah, so you're up.

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:09.910
Looks like you had a good night's sleep.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.920
Your snoring was something else.

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:16.880
It sounded like an earthquake.

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:20.330
Plates broke and the roof caved in.

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:22.750
I thought it was the end for this house.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:27.270
Kidding.

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:29.330
I'm just kidding with you!

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:42.240
Honey and Erin

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:47.960
Here, take this.

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:52.380
What are these?

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:56.620
They're safety gear to protect you from my precious treasures.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:03:00.290
When we go out to the backyard, wear that and put the gloves on.

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:01.910
What do you mean by "treasures?"

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:03.420
They're...

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.640
Well, let's just save the fun for when you see it yourself.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:17.550
On a Touda's back, Erin was carried to the land far west,

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:22.410
and was found unconscious by Jone, the honey man,

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:26.200
in the lake on the eastern end of the Queen's quarter.

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:39.030
Tocchi!  Noro!  That's not your breakfast.

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:42.760
Tocchi and...  Noro?

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:46.050
Isn't she one hot babe?

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:48.020
Look at her legs.

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:52.480
And her long eyelashes and this slender nose.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:54.440
Though, she's a bit horsey looking.

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:02.140
These are my treasures.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.270
They're honeybees!

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.120
Won't they sting you?

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:24.750
Don't worry.  My bees are raised well.

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:29.090
I bet they're just having fun dancing.

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:40.090
Hey!

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:44.600
If you approach them like that, I can't take any responsibility for what might happen to you.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:46.630
I-I'm sorry.

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:57.590
It's honey!

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:04.470
It's beautiful.

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:06.090
Take a lick.

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:17.690
How is it?

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.300
It's delicious!

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:21.810
Isn't it?

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:25.200
Fresh honey is the secret behind my beauty.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:27.790
Oh, but...

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:31.540
Hey, where are you going?

00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:42.510
I knew it.  It's not the flower's nectar.

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:48.600
Hey, what are you doing?

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:56.580
The nectar of this flower is sweet, but it tastes completely different from the honey.

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:00.520
You've got a pretty sharp mind.

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:04.110
Let's think.  What is honey?

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:09.820
Honeybees drink the nectar, take it back to the nest and spit it out,

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:13.020
so I've always thought that the bees' saliva mixes in.

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:15.770
I see.  That's a good train of thought.

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:19.180
But bees are very small.

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:26.200
If they salivated enough to make this dilute nectar that thick,

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:29.200
wouldn't that make them shrink?

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:35.430
All right.  Once we're done with the work, I'll teach you about bees.

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:47.660
From that day forward, Jone taught Erin about bees whenever he found the time.

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:56.970
He taught her names of flowers she'd never heard of and how their pollens were sweet.

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:11.130
Above all, life here was completely different than that in Ake Village.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:14.610
Every day was a new surprise.

00:07:16.510 --> 00:07:24.590
Every time Erin discovered something new and found it strange, and then gave thought to why it happened,

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:28.250
her heart was filled with excitement.

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:35.430
I wonder what happened.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:37.060
Oji-san!

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:39.690
The bees are acting strange!

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.840
Oh no, it's a colony fission.

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:03.610
Hey, don't move.

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:22.330
It's safe now.  Once they're like that, they won't stir for a while.

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:24.170
Wow.

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:26.460
Are they angry?

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:30.700
No, they're not angry.

00:08:30.890 --> 00:08:34.910
They're a colony led by a queen who left their old home.

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:42.770
When the colony becomes too big, the queen takes about half the worker bees and leaves the hive.

00:08:43.430 --> 00:08:45.900
That's what colony fission is.

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:48.650
I see.

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:52.810
That's why all those bees were outside the hive.

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:56.180
That's the sign that a colony fission is about to begin.

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:58.210
I'm amazed you noticed the difference.

00:08:58.210 --> 00:09:04.000
I was told that a nest goes through a change whenever there's a change in the animal.

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:11.030
You're a very interesting kid.

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:26.330
Watch where you step.

00:09:33.930 --> 00:09:37.870
Crap.  This is the only empty hive.

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:43.330
I'll go out with this, so you bring that out with you.

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:48.750
You mean the nebulizer?

00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:52.740
Holy cow.  You know what a nebulizer is?

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:16.880
Bring it out for me, 'kay?

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:28.550
All right, lend me that.

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:37.590
It smells good!

00:10:37.810 --> 00:10:40.740
I hope the bees think so, too.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:47.060
I get it!  You're going to lure the bees into the nest with this scent!

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:50.040
You're really quick to catch stuff.

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:53.950
But, you're WRONG!

00:10:55.410 --> 00:11:00.080
What does the attracting is the sugar water I spray after this.

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:03.040
I'm spraying this for a different reason.

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:03.970
Can you guess what it's for?

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:09.270
Probably not.

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:18.680
Just then, Erin recalled something she had seen before.

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:29.810
The first time Lulu was taken into the pond, the adults were spraying her with the other Touda's mucus.

00:11:32.780 --> 00:11:33.880
Oji-san.

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:37.170
Is that to get rid of the smell?

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:39.150
What made you think that?

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:46.620
I thought that it might be used to get rid of some smell to let them know that it's safe.

00:11:47.070 --> 00:11:48.490
You're dead on.

00:11:48.490 --> 00:11:50.330
You've really surprised me with this one.

00:11:53.110 --> 00:11:57.940
You see, a poison toad got into this one, and they're natural enemies.

00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:03.470
I have washed and dried it, but honeybees are sensitive to scents.

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:07.430
Were you keeping some animals at your old place?

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:23.320
All right, let's bring this one out to them, shall we?

00:12:56.820 --> 00:12:59.240
All right, that takes care of that.

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:00.900
Let's go have lunch.

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:06.630
Won't they run away if you leave it like that?

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:11.190
It's fine.  You'll see what I mean when we come out after lunch.

00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:12.340
But...

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:15.880
If you're that worried, then watch them until you're satisfied.

00:13:16.630 --> 00:13:22.000
I'll go get our lunch ready.  Just stay away from the hive.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:22.840
Do you understand?

00:13:23.170 --> 00:13:23.930
Yup.

00:14:24.680 --> 00:14:28.160
Are you trying to stop my heart?

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:32.120
I-I'm sorry.

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:38.030
My gosh.  You're gutsier than I thought.

00:14:38.510 --> 00:14:47.280
But I don't understand.  They left the hive, yet they've entered another one so obediently.

00:14:49.190 --> 00:14:53.430
That's because this hive has become their new home.

00:14:54.060 --> 00:14:58.640
Wherever the queen decides to live, it becomes the colony's new home.

00:15:00.410 --> 00:15:04.500
The colony's worker bees obey the queen, no matter what.

00:15:05.770 --> 00:15:10.350
You know.  All mothers have this strange power.

00:15:10.350 --> 00:15:11.730
Mother?

00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:13.860
The queen's the mother?

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:16.410
That's right.  Mother of all the bees in the colony.

00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:20.070
Sounds like a joke, right?

00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:23.250
On top of that, all the worker bees are female.

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:25.310
But they don't lay eggs.

00:15:25.310 --> 00:15:29.300
The queen lays thousands of eggs all by herself.

00:15:32.710 --> 00:15:37.610
Then, all the worker bees are directly related to the queen, right?

00:15:37.610 --> 00:15:40.190
Why can't they become the queen?

00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:44.920
Let me show you something cool.

00:15:50.990 --> 00:15:52.610
There we go.

00:15:54.290 --> 00:15:55.390
Come check this out.

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:01.330
Is that honey?

00:16:13.230 --> 00:16:14.820
Sorry about that.

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:16.510
Was it that bitter?

00:16:16.510 --> 00:16:18.890
What... is this?

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:20.850
Numbing agent.

00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:26.610
I'm just kidding with you.

00:16:26.610 --> 00:16:28.490
This is bees' milk.

00:16:28.870 --> 00:16:30.070
It's called tabchim.

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:32.170
"Tabchim?"

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:39.150
Only the larvae that are fed this tabchim, made by the worker bees, can become the queen.

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:43.210
Let me tell you something neat.

00:16:43.590 --> 00:16:46.710
I can create a queen.

00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:51.350
Grab that hive there for me.

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:55.430
Here.

00:17:00.430 --> 00:17:04.850
First, you split the box into two areas by inserting a wooden block.

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:07.190
What do you think would happen?

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:10.840
They'll panic since the queen's missing.

00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:17.450
Right then, I bring a worker bee's larva.

00:17:17.710 --> 00:17:24.190
Then the worker bees start feeding the larva with tabchim.

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:28.740
What?

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:34.610
Then the queen and the worker bees come from the same larvae?

00:17:35.500 --> 00:17:38.420
Yup.  There's only one difference.

00:17:38.420 --> 00:17:40.670
Whether it grows up drinking tabchim or not.

00:17:40.670 --> 00:17:42.660
It's almost like magic, don't you think?

00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:49.730
Oji-san, will my tongue be all right?  Will it turn into something strange?

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:55.200
I don't know.  You might have turned into a queen bee by tomorrow morning.

00:18:01.550 --> 00:18:02.620
Kidding.

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:04.150
I'm just kidding with you.

00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:10.270
But you recovered thanks to this.

00:18:11.010 --> 00:18:16.340
I was feeding you a mixture of this and orange juice when you had the fever.

00:18:16.630 --> 00:18:19.990
Guess what?  That would usually cost one small silver nugget.

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:20.680
What?!

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:23.310
O-One small silver nugget?

00:18:24.130 --> 00:18:36.260
One small silver nugget was worth enough to buy three adult's fist-sized chunks of beef, enjoyed only during festivals.

00:18:39.240 --> 00:18:40.760
Oji-san...

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:43.260
What's the matter?

00:18:43.650 --> 00:18:45.210
Are you hungry?

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:51.710
Oji-san...  I don't have any money.

00:18:53.010 --> 00:18:55.630
That was stupid of me.

00:18:55.630 --> 00:18:58.170
It was thoughtless of me to say that.

00:18:58.910 --> 00:19:02.670
I'm not thinking of taking any money from you.

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:07.730
What's wrong?  Don't worry!

00:19:07.730 --> 00:19:12.310
As long as my cute bees gather the nectar, we're good.

00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:15.780
As a pastime, I can take care of one kid like you.

00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:19.910
Crap, I just passed gas.

00:19:26.190 --> 00:19:32.910
Even in Jone's kind words, Erin couldn't take comfort.

00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:41.980
For Erin, she felt guilty being pampered for free by someone who was not her family.

00:19:43.080 --> 00:19:46.310
If she were kicked out of here...

00:19:46.890 --> 00:19:56.270
The loneliness from losing her mother and not having a place to return to would well up in her heart.

00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:06.520
Colony fission is all about the queen leaving behind the place she lived for her children,

00:20:06.900 --> 00:20:14.000
so that they can live there, and someday journey on.

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:18.810
<i>Live.  And find your happiness.</i>

00:20:21.260 --> 00:20:23.040
<i>Mom!</i>

00:20:25.610 --> 00:20:27.660
<i>Mom!</i>

00:20:40.310 --> 00:20:41.680
Oji-san.

00:20:41.680 --> 00:20:45.970
I don't have a home to return to.

00:20:46.790 --> 00:20:48.630
I don't have any money, either.

00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:52.610
But I can cook.

00:20:52.610 --> 00:20:56.210
I'm not good at it, but I can mend, too.

00:20:56.770 --> 00:20:59.010
I'll take care of Tocchi and Noro, too.

00:20:59.390 --> 00:21:01.590
I'll work hard.

00:21:01.590 --> 00:21:04.650
Please let me stay here.

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:16.370
Do you know how much an inn charges a child on a journey?

00:21:19.610 --> 00:21:26.100
Then do you know how much a child hired as an under-servant makes per day?

00:21:27.770 --> 00:21:31.090
In either case, it's about 50 bronze medals.

00:21:31.090 --> 00:21:36.480
So if you're going to take care of the house chores here, that about evens things out.

00:21:37.990 --> 00:21:40.350
What do you think of that as a deal?

00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:47.470
All right!  Looks like we have a deal!

00:21:47.470 --> 00:21:49.950
Make sure you work hard starting tomorrow.

00:21:50.550 --> 00:21:52.270
Eh...

00:21:52.670 --> 00:21:53.870
It's Erin!

00:21:54.420 --> 00:21:57.290
"Erin," as in "wild apple," eh?

00:21:57.630 --> 00:22:00.020
It's small, but it's red and cute.

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:02.670
It's a perfect name for you.

00:22:04.930 --> 00:22:06.570
I'm Jone.

00:22:06.570 --> 00:22:07.820
The honey man.

00:22:13.370 --> 00:22:15.330
Erin made a decision.

00:22:16.460 --> 00:22:26.220
She decided to live strongly to the best of her ability in this world where her mother left her, just like these bees.

00:24:02.730 --> 00:24:06.240
It's the Sezans' duty to live as the Queen's shield.

00:24:07.830 --> 00:24:14.580
Hearing the news that a Touda egg thief could be hiding in the town of Salim, I venture with a harp in hand.

00:24:15.380 --> 00:24:20.340
However, what appears before me
is a girl with green eyes.

00:24:21.040 --> 00:24:25.030
Kemono no Souja Erin.  Bird of Dawn.

00:24:25.030 --> 00:24:25.050
Bird of Dawn
Kemono no Souja Erin.  Bird of Dawn.

00:24:25.050 --> 00:24:30.030
Bird of Dawn
